Alternatively, perhaps there is a different way to model it. Maybe considering the complement of the problem.

Let me think about the individual collections. Each person has a subset of the n stickers, but not all. Let me think of each person's collection as a subset S_i of {1, 2, ..., n}, where none of the S_i's is equal to the full set.

A pair of friends is wholesome if S_i ∪ S_j = {1, 2, ..., n}. Therefore, their union is the entire set.

So, if we think of each person's collection as a subset, then the complement of their collection is the set of stickers they are missing. Let me define for each person, the complement set C_i = {1, 2, ..., n} \ S_i. Since S_i is not the full set, C_i is non-empty.

